3.8.1 Libraries in the SINGULAR Documentation
---------------------------------------------

   * The typesetting language in which the SINGULAR documentation is
     written is `texinfo'. The info string of a library included in the
     SINGULAR distribution will be parsed and automatically translated
     to the `texinfo' format. The same applies to the help string of
     each procedure listed in the PROCEDURE: section of the info string.

   * Based on various tools, `info', `dvi', `p', and `html' versions of
     the `texinfo' documentation are generated.

   * For texinfo markup elements and other information facilitating
     optimal typesetting, see *note Typesetting of help and info
     strings::.

   * For the convenience of users checking directly the source code, the
     `texinfo'  tools should be used economically. That is, the info
     and  help texts should be well readable verbatim.

   * The example of each procedure listed in the PROCEDURE: section of
     the info string is computed and its output is included in the
     documentation.


