4.3.3 bigintmat type cast
-------------------------

`*Syntax:*'
     `bigintmat (' expression `)'

`*Type:*'
     bigintmat

`*Purpose:*'
     Converts expression to a bigintmat, where expression must be of
     type intmat, bigintvec, or bigintmat.The size (resp. dimension) of
     the created bigintmat equals the size (resp. dimension) of the
     expression.

`*Example:*'
            intmat im[2][1]=2, 3;
            bigintmat(im);
          ==> 2,
          ==> 3
            bigintmat(_);
          ==> 2,
          ==> 3
            bigintmat(intmat(intvec(1,2,3,4), 2, 2)); //casts at first to intmat, then to bigintmat
          ==> 1,2,
          ==> 3,4

