4.10.1 link declarations
------------------------

*Syntax:*
     `link' name `=' string_expression `;'

*Purpose:*
     defines a new communication link.

*Default:*
     none

*Example:*
            link l=":w example.txt";
            int i=22;          // cf. ASCII links for explanation
            string s="An int follows:";
            write(l,s,i);
            l;
          ==> // type : ASCII
          ==> // mode : w
          ==> // name : example.txt
          ==> // open : yes
          ==> // read : not ready
          ==> // write: ready
            close(l);          //
            read(l);
          ==> An int follows:
          ==> 22
          ==>
            close(l);


