4.11.1 list declarations
------------------------

*Syntax:*
     `list' name `=' expression_list`;'
     `list' name `=' list_expression`;'

*Purpose:*
     defines a list (of objects of possibly different types).

*Default:*
     empty list

*Example:*
            list l=1,"str";
            l[1];
          ==> 1
            l[2];
          ==> str
            ring r;
            listvar(r);
          ==> // r                              [0]  *ring
            ideal i = x^2, y^2 + z^3;
            l[3] = i;
            l;
          ==> [1]:
          ==>    1
          ==> [2]:
          ==>    str
          ==> [3]:
          ==>    _[1]=x2
          ==>    _[2]=z3+y2
            listvar(r);     // the list l belongs now to the ring r
          ==> // r                              [0]  *ring
          ==> // l                              [0]  list, size: 3
          ==> // i                              [0]  ideal, 2 generator(s)


