4.14.1 module declarations
--------------------------

*Syntax:*
     `module' name `=' list_of_vector_expressions `;'
     `module' name `=' module_expression `;'

*Purpose:*
     defines a module.

*Default:*
     [0]

*Example:*
            ring r=0,(x,y,z),(c,dp);
            vector s1 = [x2,y3,z];
            vector s2 = [xy,1,0];
            vector s3 = [0,x2-y2,z];
            poly   f  = xyz;
            module m = s1, s2-s1,f*(s3-s1);
            m;
          ==> m[1]=[x2,y3,z]
          ==> m[2]=[-x2+xy,-y3+1,-z]
          ==> m[3]=[-x3yz,-xy4z+x3yz-xy3z]
            // show m in matrix format (columns generate m)
            print(m);
          ==> x2,-x2+xy,-x3yz,
          ==> y3,-y3+1, -xy4z+x3yz-xy3z,
          ==> z, -z,    0


