4.21 smatrix
============

An experimental type:
Objects of type smatrix are (sparse) matrices with polynomial entries.
Like polynomials they can only be defined or accessed with respect to a
basering.

Objects of type `smatrix' can be converted to and from `matrix' and
`module'.
Operations are `+', `-', `*', `==', `<>'.
Functions are `chinrem', `farey', `ncols', `nrows', `std', `transpose',
`tensor'.  Additional `flatten(m)' and `system("unflatten",m,col)'.
Resizing can be done via `smatrix(m,r,c)' where m is of type `module'
or `smatrix'.
Access to single entries: `m[i,j]'

