4.24 User defined types
=======================

User defined types are (non-empty) lists with a fixed size whose
element can be accessed by names (and not indices).  These elements
have a predefined type (which can also be a user defined type).  If
these elements depend on a ring they can only be accessed if their base
ring is the current base ring.  In contrast to usual lists the elements
of a user defined type may belong to different rings.

* Menu:

* Definition of a user defined type::
