5.1.120 print
-------------

`*Syntax:*'
     `print (' expression `)'
     `print (' expression`, "betti" )'
     `print (' expression`,' format_string `)'

`*Type:*'
     string

`*Purpose:*'
     The first form prints the expression.
     The second form prints the graded Betti numbers from a matrix.
     The Betti numbers are printed in a matrix-like format where the
     entry d in row i and column j is the minimal number of generators
     in degree i+j of the j-th  syzygy module of R^n/M (the 0th and 1st
     syzygy module of R^n/M are R^n and M, resp.).
     The last form returns the printed output as a string depending on
     the format string iwhich determines the format to use to generate
     the string.

     The following format strings are supported:
    `"%s"'
          returns `string(' expression `)',

    `"%2s"'
          similar to `"%s"', except that newlines are inserted after
          every comma and at the end,

    `"%l"'
          similar to `"%s"', except that each object is embraced by its
          type such that it can be directly used for "cutting and
          pasting",

    `"%2l"'
          similar to `"%l"', except that newlines are inserted after
          every comma and at the end,

    `"%;"'
          returns the string equivalent to typing `expression;'

    `"%t"'
          returns the string equivalent to typing `type expression;'

    `"%p"'
          returns the string equivalent to typing `print(expression);'

    `"%b"'
          returns the string equivalent to typing `print(expression,
          "betti");'

    `"betti"'
          is not a format string.

`*Example:*'
            ring r=0,(x,y,z),dp;
            module m=[1,y],[0,x+z];
            m;
          ==> m[1]=y*gen(2)+gen(1)
          ==> m[2]=x*gen(2)+z*gen(2)
            print(m);  // the columns generate m
          ==> 1,0,
          ==> y,x+z
            string s=print(m,"%s"); s;
          ==> y*gen(2)+gen(1),x*gen(2)+z*gen(2)
            s=print(m,"%2s"); s;
          ==> y*gen(2)+gen(1),
          ==> x*gen(2)+z*gen(2)
          ==>
            s=print(m,"%l"); s;
          ==> module(y*gen(2)+gen(1),x*gen(2)+z*gen(2))
            s=print(m,"%;"); s;
          ==> m[1]=y*gen(2)+gen(1)
          ==> m[2]=x*gen(2)+z*gen(2)
          ==>
            s=print(m,"%t"); s;
          ==> // m module , rk 2
          ==> m[1]=y*gen(2)+gen(1)
          ==> m[2]=x*gen(2)+z*gen(2)
            s=print(m,"%p"); s;
          ==> 1,0,
          ==> y,x+z
            intmat M=betti(mres(m,0));
            print(M,"betti");
          ==>            0     1
          ==> ------------------
          ==>     0:     1     1
          ==> ------------------
