5.1.129 rank
------------

`*Syntax:*'
     `rank (' matrix_expression `)' #*`rank (' matrix_expression `,1)'

`*Type:*'
     int

`*Purpose:*'
     returns the rank of a given matrix which is filled with elements
     of the ground field.
     The first variant uses a LU-decomposition, the second a
     row-echelon form.

`*Note_*'
     The function works by computing the row echelon form of the matrix
     using the same algorithm as for `ludecomp'.

`*Example:*'
            ring s = 0, x, dp;
            matrix A[100][100];
            int i; int j; int r;
            for (i = 1; i <= 100; i++)
            {
              for (j = 1; j <= 100; j++)
              {
                A[i, j] = random(-10, 10);
              }
            }
            r = rank(A); r;
          ==> 100

