5.1.146 sortvec
---------------

`*Syntax:*'
     `sortvec (' ideal_expression `)'
     `sortvec (' module_expression `)'

`*Type:*'
     intvec

`*Purpose:*'
     computes the permutation v which orders the ideal, resp. module, I
     by its initial terms, starting with the smallest, that is,
     I(v[i]) < I(v[i+1]) for all i.

`*Example:*'
            ring r=0,(x,y,z),dp;
            ideal I=y,z,x,x3,xz;
