`*Type:*'
     matrix

`*Purpose:*'
     `wedge(M,n)' computes the `n'-th exterior power of the matrix `M'.

`*Example:*'
            ring r;
            matrix m[2][3]=x,y,y,z,z,x;
            print(m);
          ==> x,y,y,
          ==> z,z,x
            print(wedge(m,2));
          ==> xz-yz,-x2+yz,xy-yz

