5.2.1 apply
-----------

`*Syntax:*'
     `apply(' expression `,' function `);'

`*Purpose:*'
     applies the function to all elements of the first argument.  The
     first argument must be of type `intvec', `intmat', or `list'.  The
     result will be an expression list, its type and format will be set
     by the following assign.  The function must be a kernel command or
     a procedure which takes one argument and returns a a value.

`*Example:*'
          proc p(int x) {return(x^2);}
          intvec v=1,2,3;
          apply(v,p);
          ==> 1 4 9
          intvec vv=apply(v,p);vv;
          ==> 1,4,9
          list ll=apply(v,p);ll;
          ==> [1]:
          ==>    1
          ==> [2]:
          ==>    4
          ==> [3]:
          ==>    9


