5.2.5 else
----------

`*Syntax:*'
     `if (' boolean_expression `)' true_block `else' false_block

`*Purpose:*'
     executes false_block if the boolean_expression of the `if'
     statement is false. This command is only valid in combination with
     an `if' command.

`*Example:*'
          int i=3;
          if (i > 5)
          {
            "i is bigger than 5";
          }
          else
          {
            "i is smaller than 6";
          }
          ==> i is smaller than 6

