7.5.1.1 bistd
.............

Procedure from library `bimodules.lib' (*note bimodules_lib::).

*Usage:*
     bistd(M); M is (two-sided) ideal/module

*Return:*
     ideal or module (same type as the argument)

*Purpose:*
     Computes the two-sided Groebner basis of an ideal/module with the
     help the enveloping algebra of the basering, alternative to
     twostd() for ideals.

*Example:*
     LIB "bimodules.lib";
     ring w = 0,(x,s),Dp;
     def W=nc_algebra(1,s); // 1st shift algebra
     setring W;
     matrix m[3][3]=[s^2,s+1,0],[s+1,0,s^3-x^2*s],[2*s+1, s^3+s^2, s^2];
     print(m);
     ==> s2,   s+1,    s+1,
     ==> 0,    -x2s+s3,2s+1,
     ==> s3+s2,s2,     0
     module L = m; module M2 = bistd(L);
     print(M2);
     ==> 1,1,s+1,
     ==> 0,1,0,
     ==> 0,0,s2


