7.5.6.6 annfalphaI
..................

Procedure from library `dmodideal.lib' (*note dmodideal_lib::).

*Usage:*
     annfalphaI(f,alpha); f,alpha ideals

*Return:*
     ring

*Assume:*
     basering is a commutative polynomial ring in characteristic 0

*Purpose:*
     determine annihilator of f^alpha with the method of (OT99)

*Note_*
     The returned ring contains the annihilator of f^alpha over D as
     annfalpha.  alpha should contain the desired rational exponents.
     The procedure may also be applied to the univariate case, i.e. for
     r=1.

*Example:*
     LIB "dmodideal.lib";
     ring R = 0,(x,y,z),dp;
     ideal f = x,y,z;
     ideal alpha = 1/4, 2/3, 1;
     def A = annfalphaI(f,alpha);
     setring A;
     annfalpha;
     ==> annfalpha[1]=Dz^2
     ==> annfalpha[2]=z*Dz-1
     ==> annfalpha[3]=3*y*Dy-2
     ==> annfalpha[4]=4*x*Dx-1


