7.5.16.6 is_cenBimodule
.......................

Procedure from library `nchomolog.lib' (*note nchomolog_lib::).

*Usage:*
     is_cenBimodule(M); M module

*Compute:*
     1, if a module, presented by M can be centralizing in the sense of
     Artin and 0 otherwise

*Note_*
     only one condition for centralizing factor module can be checked
     algorithmically

*Example:*
     LIB "nchomolog.lib";
     def A = makeUsl2(); setring A;
     poly p = 4*e*f + h^2-2*h; // generator of the center
     matrix M[2][2] = p, p^2-7,0,p*(p+1);
     is_cenBimodule(M); // M is centralizing
     ==> 1
     matrix N[2][2] = p, e*f,h,p*(p+1);
     is_cenBimodule(N); // N is not centralizing
     ==> 0


