7.5.19.4 isUpperTriangular
..........................

Procedure from library `ncpreim.lib' (*note ncpreim_lib::).

*Usage:*
     isUpperTriangular(M[,k]); M a matrix, k an optional int

*Return:*
     int, 1 if the given matrix is upper triangular,
     0 otherwise.

*Note_*
     If k<>0 is given, it is checked whether M is strictly upper
     triangular.

*Example:*
     LIB "ncpreim.lib";
     ring r = 0,x,dp;
     matrix M[2][3] =
     0,1,2,
     0,0,3;
     isUpperTriangular(M);
     ==> 1
     isUpperTriangular(M,1);
     ==> 1
     M[2,2] = 4;
     isUpperTriangular(M);
     ==> 1
     isUpperTriangular(M,1);
     ==> 0


