7.5.20.10 rightStd
..................

Procedure from library `nctools.lib' (*note nctools_lib::).

*Purpose:*
     compute a right Groebner basis of I

*Return:*
     the same type as input

*Example:*
     LIB "nctools.lib";
     LIB "ncalg.lib";
     def A = makeUsl(2);
     setring A;
     ideal I = e2,f;
     option(redSB);
     option(redTail);
     ideal LI = std(I);
     LI;
     ==> LI[1]=f
     ==> LI[2]=h2+h
     ==> LI[3]=eh+e
     ==> LI[4]=e2
     ideal RI = rightStd(I);
     RI;
     ==> RI[1]=f
     ==> RI[2]=h2-h
     ==> RI[3]=eh+e
     ==> RI[4]=e2


