7.5.20.15 isCentral
...................

Procedure from library `nctools.lib' (*note nctools_lib::).

*Usage:*
     isCentral(p); p poly

*Return:*
     int, 1 if p commutes with all variables and 0 otherwise

*Purpose:*
     check whether p is central in a basering (that is, commutes with
     every generator of the ring)

*Note_*
     if `printlevel' > 0, the procedure displays intermediate
     information (by default, `printlevel'=0 )

*Example:*
     LIB "nctools.lib";
     ring r=0,(x,y,z),dp;
     matrix D[3][3]=0;
     D[1,2]=-z;
     D[1,3]=2*x;
     D[2,3]=-2*y;
     def S = nc_algebra(1,D); setring S;
     S; // this is U(sl_2)
     ==> // coefficients: QQ considered as a field
     ==> // number of vars : 3
     ==> //        block   1 : ordering dp
     ==> //                  : names    x y z
     ==> //        block   2 : ordering C
     ==> // noncommutative relations:
     ==> //    yx=xy-z
     ==> //    zx=xz+2x
     ==> //    zy=yz-2y
     poly c = 4*x*y+z^2-2*z;
     printlevel = 0;
     isCentral(c);
     ==> 1
     poly h = x*c;
     printlevel = 1;
     isCentral(h);
     ==> Non-central at: y
     ==> Non-central at: z
     ==> 0


