7.8.10 rightstd (letterplace)
-----------------------------

`*Syntax:*'
     `rightstd(' ideal_expression`)';   `rightstd('
     module_expression`)';

`*Type:*'
     ideal or module

`*Purpose:*'
     Compute a right Groebner basis of the set of generators of the
     input ideal/module.

`*Note_*'
     It is also effective in factor rings.

`*Example:*'
          LIB "freegb.lib";
          ring r = 0,(x,z),dp;
          ring R = freeAlgebra(r,7);
          ideal I = z, x*z, x*x*z;
          rightstd(I); // a right GB of I in K<x,z>
          ==> _[1]=z
          ==> _[2]=x*z
          ==> _[3]=x*x*z
          qring Q = twostd(x*z); // now we change to the factor algebra modulo x*z
          ideal I = imap(R,I);
          rightstd(I); // a right GB in a factor algebra
          ==> _[1]=z
          reduce(I,twostd(0)); // an explanation for the latter
          ==> _[1]=z
          ==> _[2]=0
          ==> _[3]=0


