A.2 Computing Groebner and Standard Bases
=========================================

* Menu:

* groebner and std::
* Groebner basis conversion::
* slim Groebner bases::

Several operations with ideals resp. modules uses Groebner bases to
compute their result.  Most allow an optional string argument to select
the algorithm.  The possible arguments for the algorithm are
   * `default'

   * `std' see *note std::

   * `slimgb' see *note slimgb::

   * `sba' see *note sba::; not for module operations

   * `singmatic' Requires `singmatic.so'

   * `groebner' see *note groebner::

   * `modstd' see *note modStd::. Requires *note modstd_lib::

   * `ffmod' see *note ffmodStd::, Requires  *note ffmodstd_lib::

   * `nfmod' see *note nfmodStd::. Requires *note nfmodstd_lib::

   * `std:sat' Uses `satstd' instead of `std', see *note satstd::.
     Requires *note customstd_lib::

Functions with such a choice of the algorithm:
   * *note eliminate::

   * *note intersect::

   * *note modulo::

   * *note liftstd::

   * *note syz::


