D.2.3.2 A_Z_L
.............

Procedure from library `general.lib' (*note general_lib::).

*Usage:*
     A_Z_L("a",n); a any letter, n integer (-26<= n <=26, !=0)

*Return:*
     list of n small (if a is small) or capital (if a is capital)
     letters, beginning with a, in alphabetical
     order (or reverse alphabetical order if n<0)

*Example:*
     LIB "general.lib";
     A_Z_L("c",5);
     ==> [1]:
     ==>    c
     ==> [2]:
     ==>    d
     ==> [3]:
     ==>    e
     ==> [4]:
     ==>    f
     ==> [5]:
     ==>    g
     A_Z_L("Z",-5);
     ==> [1]:
     ==>    Z
     ==> [2]:
     ==>    Y
     ==> [3]:
     ==>    X
     ==> [4]:
     ==>    W
     ==> [5]:
     ==>    V
     ring r;
     list L=list(0,A_Z_L("A",6),list(list("dp",1:6),list("C",0)),ideal(0));
     ring R=ring(L);
     R;
     ==> // coefficients: QQ considered as a field
     ==> // number of vars : 6
     ==> //        block   1 : ordering dp
     ==> //                  : names    A B C D E F
     ==> //        block   2 : ordering C


