D.2.4.7 PtoCrep
...............

Procedure from library `grobcov.lib' (*note grobcov_lib::).

*Usage:*
     PtoCrep(list L)
     list L= [ Comp_1, .. , Comp_s ] where
     list Comp_i=[p_i,[p_i1,..,p_is_i] ], is the
     P-representation of a locally closed set
     V(N) \ V(M). To be called in a ring Q[a][x]
     or a ring Q[a]. But the ideals can contain
     only the parameters in Q[a].

*Return:*
     The canonical C-representation [P,Q] of the
     locally closed set. A pair of radical ideals with
     P included in Q, representing the
     set V(P) \ V(Q)

*Example:*
     LIB "grobcov.lib";
     //EXAMPLE:
     if(defined(R)){kill R;}
     ring R=0,(a,b,c),lp;
     short=0;
     ideal p=a*(a^2+b^2+c^2-25);
     ideal q=a*(a-3),b-4;
     // C-representaion of V(p) \ V(q)
     def Cr=Crep(p,q);
     Cr;
     ==> [1]:
     ==>    _[1]=a^3+a*b^2+a*c^2-25*a
     ==> [2]:
     ==>    _[1]=b-4
     ==>    _[2]=a*c
     ==>    _[3]=a^2-3*a
     // P-representation of V(p) \ V(q)
     def L=Prep(p,q);
     L;
     ==> [1]:
     ==>    [1]:
     ==>       _[1]=a^2+b^2+c^2-25
     ==>    [2]:
     ==>       [1]:
     ==>          _[1]=c-3
     ==>          _[2]=b-4
     ==>          _[3]=a
     ==>       [2]:
     ==>          _[1]=c+3
     ==>          _[2]=b-4
     ==>          _[3]=a
     ==>       [3]:
     ==>          _[1]=c
     ==>          _[2]=b-4
     ==>          _[3]=a-3
     ==> [2]:
     ==>    [1]:
     ==>       _[1]=a
     ==>    [2]:
     ==>       [1]:
     ==>          _[1]=b-4
     ==>          _[2]=a
     PtoCrep(L);
     ==> [1]:
     ==>    _[1]=a^3+a*b^2+a*c^2-25*a
     ==> [2]:
     ==>    _[1]=b-4
     ==>    _[2]=a*c
     ==>    _[3]=a^2-3*a


