D.2.4.14 stdlocus
.................

Procedure from library `grobcov.lib' (*note grobcov_lib::).

*Usage:*
     stdlocus(ideal F)
     The input ideal must be the set equations defining the locus.
     Calling sequence: locus(F);
     The input ring must be a parametrical ideal in Q[x][u], (x=tracer
     variables, u=remaining variables).
     (Inverts the concept of parameters and variables of the ring).
     Special routine for determining the locus of points of a
     geometrical construction.  Given a parametric ideal F representing
     the system determining the locus of points (x) which verify
     certain properties, the call to stdlocus(F) determines the
     different irreducible components of the locus.  This is a simple
     routine, using only standard Groebner basis computation,
     elimination and prime decomposition instead of using grobcov.  It
     does not determine the taxonomy, nor the holes of the components

*Return:*
     The output is a list of the tops of the components [C_1, .. , C_n]
     of the locus.  Each component is given its top ideal p_i.

*Note_*
     The input must be the locus system.

*Example:*
     LIB "grobcov.lib";
     if(defined(R)){kill R;}
     ring R=(0,x,y),(x1,y1),dp;
     short=0;
     // Concoid
     ideal S96=x1 ^2+y1 ^2-4,(x-2)*x1 -x*y1 +2*x,(x-x1 )^2+(y-y1 )^2-1;
     stdlocus(S96);
     ==> [1]:
     ==>    _[1]=(x^4+2*x^3+x^2*y^2-3*x^2-2*x*y^2-8*x*y-6*x+2*y^2+8*y+6)
     ==> [2]:
     ==>    _[1]=(x^2+y^2-4*y+3)


