D.2.4.17 discrim
................

Procedure from library `grobcov.lib' (*note grobcov_lib::).

*Usage:*
     discrim(f,x);
     poly f: the polynomial in Q[a][x] or Q[x] of degree 2 in x poly x:
     can be a variable or a parameter of the ring.

*Return:*
     the factorized discriminant of f wrt x for discussing its sign

*Example:*
     LIB "grobcov.lib";
     if(defined(R)){kill R;}
     ring R=(0,a,b,c),(x,y),dp;
     short=0;
     poly f=a*x^2*y+b*x*y+c*y;
     discrim(f,x);
     ==> [1]:
     ==>    _[1]=-1
     ==>    _[2]=(4*a*c-b^2)
     ==>    _[3]=y
     ==> [2]:
     ==>    1,1,2


