D.2.12 ring_lib
---------------

*Library:*
     ring.lib

*Purpose:*
     Manipulating Rings and Maps

*Authors:*
     Singular team


*Procedures:*

* Menu:

* changechar:: make a copy of basering [ring r] with new char c
* changeord:: make a copy of basering [ring r] with new ord o
* changevar:: make a copy of basering [ring r] with new vars v
* defring:: define a ring R in specified char c, n vars v, ord o
* defrings:: define ring Sn in n vars, char 32003 [p], ord ds
* defringp:: define ring Pn in n vars, char 32003 [p], ord dp
* extendring:: extend given ring by n vars v, ord o and name it R
* fetchall:: fetch all objects of ring R to basering
* imapall:: imap all objects of ring R to basering
* mapall:: map all objects of ring R via ideal i to basering
* ord_test:: test whether ordering of R is global, local or mixed
* ringtensor:: create ring, tensor product of rings s,t,...
* ringweights:: intvec of weights of ring variables of ring r
* preimageLoc:: computes preimage for non-global orderings
* rootofUnity:: the minimal polynomial for the n-th primitive root of unity (parameters in square brackets [] are optional)
* optionIsSet:: check if as a string given option is set or not. hasFieldCoefficient check if the coefficient ring is considered a field hasGFCoefficient check if the coefficient ring is GF(p,k) hasZpCoefficient check if the coefficient ring is ZZ/p hasZp_aCoefficient check if the coefficient ring is an elag. ext. of ZZ/p hasQQCoefficient check if the coefficient ring is QQ
* hasNumericCoeffs:: check for use of floating point numbers
* hasCommutativeVars:: non-commutative or commutative polynomial ring
* hasGlobalOrdering:: global versus mixed/local monomial ordering
* hasMixedOrdering:: mixed versus global/local ordering
* hasAlgExtensionCoefficient:: coefficients are an algebraic extension
* hasTransExtensionCoefficient:: coefficients are rational functions
* isQuotientRing:: ring is a qotient ring
* isSubModule:: check if I is in J as submodule
* changeordTo:: change the ordering of a ring to a simple one
* addvarsTo:: add variables to a ring
* addNvarsTo:: add N variables to a ring


