D.2.12.15 rootofUnity
.....................

Procedure from library `ring.lib' (*note ring_lib::).

*Usage:*
     rootofUnity(n); n an integer

*Return:*
     number

*Purpose:*
     compute the minimal polynomial for the n-th primitive root of unity

*Note_*
     works only in field extensions by one element

*Example:*
     LIB "ring.lib";
     ring r = (0,q),(x,y,z),dp;
     rootofUnity(6);
     ==> (q2-q+1)
     rootofUnity(7);
     ==> (q6+q5+q4+q3+q2+q+1)
     minpoly = rootofUnity(8);
     r;
     ==> // coefficients: QQ[q]/(q4+1) considered as a field
     ==> // number of vars : 3
     ==> //        block   1 : ordering dp
     ==> //                  : names    x y z
     ==> //        block   2 : ordering C


