D.2.13.3 copyTask
.................

Procedure from library `tasks.lib' (*note tasks_lib::).

*Usage:*
     copyTask(t), t task

*Return:*
     a copy of t.

*Note_*
     'task t1 = copyTask(t2);' is not the same as 'task t1 = t2;'. After
     the latter command, t1 points to the same object as t2; any changes
     to t2 will also effect t1. In contrast to this, copyTask() creates
     a new independent task.
     A task whose state is 'started' cannot be copied.

*Example:*
     LIB "tasks.lib";
     ring R = 0, (x,y), dp;
     ideal I = x9y2+x10, x2y7-y8;
     task t1 = "std", list(I);
     startTasks(t1);
     waitAllTasks(t1);
     task t2 = copyTask(t1);
     killTask(t1);
     t2;   // t2 survived
     ==> A task with the following properties:
     ==> command:          std
     ==> no. of arguments: 1
     ==> state:            completed
     ==>
     getResult(t2);
     ==> _[1]=x2y7-y8
     ==> _[2]=x9y2+x10
     ==> _[3]=x12y+xy11
     ==> _[4]=x13-xy12
     ==> _[5]=y14+xy12
     ==> _[6]=xy13+y12
     killTask(t2);

* Menu:

See also:
* compareTasks::
* createTask::
* getArguments::
* getCommand::
* getResult::
* getState::
* killTask::
* printTask::


