D.2.13.9 waitAllTasks
.....................

Procedure from library `tasks.lib' (*note tasks_lib::).

*Usage:*
     waitAllTasks(t1, t2, ...), t1, t2, ... tasks

*Return:*
     nothing. Waits for all the tasks t1, t2, ... to complete. The state
     of the tasks is set to 'completed'.

*Note_*
     A task whose state is neither 'started' nor 'completed' cannot be
     waited for.
     The result of any completed task can be accessed via *note
     getResult::.
     'waitAllTasks(t1, t2, ...);' is a shortcut for 'waitTasks(list(t1,
     t2, ...), size(list(t1, t2, ...)));'. Since returning a list of
     the indices of the completed tasks does not make sense in this
     case, nothing is returned.

*Example:*
     LIB "tasks.lib";
     ring R = 0, (x,y), dp;
     ideal I = x9y2+x10, x2y7-y8;
     task t1 = "std", list(I);
     task t2 = "slimgb", list(I);
     startTasks(t1, t2);
     waitAllTasks(t1, t2);   // the same as 'waitTasks(list(t1, t2), 2);',
     // but without return value
     getResult(t1);
     ==> _[1]=x2y7-y8
     ==> _[2]=x9y2+x10
     ==> _[3]=x12y+xy11
     ==> _[4]=x13-xy12
     ==> _[5]=y14+xy12
     ==> _[6]=xy13+y12
     getResult(t2);
     ==> _[1]=x2y7-y8
     ==> _[2]=x9y2+x10
     ==> _[3]=x12y+xy11
     ==> _[4]=x13-xy12
     ==> _[5]=xy13+y12
     ==> _[6]=y14+xy12
     killTask(t1);
     killTask(t2);

