*Usage:*
     getResult(t), t task

*Return:*
     the result of t.

*Note_*
     This command cannot be applied to tasks whose state is not
     'completed'.

*Example:*
     LIB "tasks.lib";
     ring R = 0, (x,y), dp;
     ideal I = x9y2+x10, x2y7-y8;
     task t = "std", list(I);
     startTasks(t);
     waitAllTasks(t);
     getResult(t);
     ==> _[1]=x2y7-y8
     ==> _[2]=x9y2+x10
     ==> _[3]=x12y+xy11
     ==> _[4]=x13-xy12
     ==> _[5]=y14+xy12
     ==> _[6]=xy13+y12
     killTask(t);

