D.3.2.2 inverse_B
.................

Procedure from library `linalg.lib' (*note linalg_lib::).

*Usage:*
     inverse_B(A); A = square matrix

*Return:*
     list Inv with
     - Inv[1] = matrix I and
     - Inv[2] = poly p
     such that I*A = unitmat(n)*p;

*Note_*
     p=1 if 1/det(A) is computable and p=det(A) if not;
     the computation uses busadj.

*Example:*
     LIB "linalg.lib";
     ring r=0,(x,y),lp;
     matrix A[3][3]=x,y,1,1,x2,y,x,6,0;
     print(A);
     ==> x,y, 1,
     ==> 1,x2,y,
     ==> x,6, 0
     list Inv=inverse_B(A);
     print(Inv[1]);
     ==> 6y,  -6,    x2-y2,
     ==> -xy, x,     xy-1,
     ==> x3-6,-xy+6x,-x3+y
     print(Inv[2]);
     ==> x3-xy2+6xy-6
     print(Inv[1]*A);
     ==> x3-xy2+6xy-6,0,           0,
     ==> 0,           x3-xy2+6xy-6,0,
     ==> 0,           0,           x3-xy2+6xy-6

* Menu:

See also:
* inverse::
* inverse_L::


