D.4.11.7 fitting
................

Procedure from library `homolog.lib' (*note homolog_lib::).

*Usage:*
     fitting (M,n); M module, n int

*Return:*
     ideal, (standard basis of) n-th Fitting ideal of M'=coker(M).

*Example:*
     LIB "homolog.lib";
     ring R=0,x(0..4),dp;
     matrix M[2][4]=x(0),x(1),x(2),x(3),x(1),x(2),x(3),x(4);
     print(M);
     ==> x(0),x(1),x(2),x(3),
     ==> x(1),x(2),x(3),x(4)
     fitting(M,-1);
     ==> _[1]=0
     fitting(M,0);
     ==> _[1]=x(3)^2-x(2)*x(4)
     ==> _[2]=x(2)*x(3)-x(1)*x(4)
     ==> _[3]=x(1)*x(3)-x(0)*x(4)
     ==> _[4]=x(2)^2-x(0)*x(4)
     ==> _[5]=x(1)*x(2)-x(0)*x(3)
     ==> _[6]=x(1)^2-x(0)*x(2)
     fitting(M,1);
     ==> _[1]=x(4)
     ==> _[2]=x(3)
     ==> _[3]=x(2)
     ==> _[4]=x(1)
     ==> _[5]=x(0)
     fitting(M,2);
     ==> _[1]=1


