D.4.16.26 compareModules
........................

Procedure from library `modules.lib' (*note modules_lib::).

*Usage:*
     compareModules(M,N); or M==N; compares two Modules up to
     isomorphism

*Return:*
     1 or 0, if the are ismomophic or aren't

*Example:*
     LIB "modules.lib";
     ring r;
     matrix ma[2][2]=x,y,x,y;
     Matrix m=ma;
     Module M=image(m);
     matrix na[2][1]=-y,x;
     Matrix n=na;
     M;
     ==> image | x y |
     ==>       | x y |
     ==>
     ==>
     Module N=image(n);
     N;
     ==> image | -y |
     ==>       | x  |
     ==>
     ==>
     N==M;
     ==> 0
     N=coker(n);
     N;
     ==> cokernel | -y |
     ==>          | x  |
     ==>
     ==>
     N==M;
     ==> 0


