D.4.24.7 genus
..............

Procedure from library `normal.lib' (*note normal_lib::).

*Return:*
     an integer, the geometric genus p_g = p_a - delta of the projective
     curve defined by i, where p_a is the arithmetic genus.

*Note_*
     genus always treats projective curves and takes projective closure
     if input is affine 1-dim variety.  delta is the sum of all local
     delta-invariants of the singularities, i.e. dim(R'/R), R' the
     normalization of the local ring R of the singularity.
     genus(I,"nor") uses the normalization to compute delta. Usually
     genus(I,"nor") is slower than genus(I) but sometimes not.
     genus(I,"pri") starts with a primary decompsition.

*Example:*
     LIB "normal.lib";
     ring r=0,(x,y),dp;
     ideal i=y^9 - x^2*(x - 1)^9;
     genus(i);
     ==> 0
     ring r7=7,(x,y),dp;
     ideal i=y^9 - x^2*(x - 1)^9;
     genus(i);
     ==> 0


