     some other data may be contained in files that you can read into
     Singular (see *note showNuminvs::, *note exportNuminvs::).

*Background:*

*Note_*
     The function also gives an error message if the matrix V has the
     wrong number of columns.

*Example:*
     LIB "normaliz.lib";
     ring R=0,(x,y,z,w),dp;
     intmat V[2][5]=0,1,2,3,4, -1,1,2,1,3;
     intersectionValRingIdeals(V);
     ==> [1]:
     ==>    _[1]=w
     ==>    _[2]=z
     ==>    _[3]=y
     ==>    _[4]=xw
     ==>    _[5]=xz
     ==>    _[6]=xy
     ==>    _[7]=x2z
     ==> [2]:
     ==>    _[1]=w3
     ==>    _[2]=zw
     ==>    _[3]=z2
     ==>    _[4]=yw2
     ==>    _[5]=y2w
     ==>    _[6]=y2z
     ==>    _[7]=y4
     ==>    _[8]=xz2
     ==>    _[9]=xy2z
     ==>    _[10]=xy4

