D.4.27.1 Ann
............

Procedure from library `primdec.lib' (*note primdec_lib::).

*Usage:*
     Ann(M); M module

*Return:*
     ideal, the annihilator of coker(M)

*Note_*
     The output is the ideal of all elements a of the basering R such
     that a * R^m is contained in M (m=number of rows of M).

*Example:*
     LIB "primdec.lib";
     ring  r = 0,(x,y,z),lp;
     module M = x2-y2,z3;
     Ann(M);
     ==> _[1]=z3
     ==> _[2]=x2-y2
     M = [1,x2],[y,x];
     Ann(M);
     ==> _[1]=x2y-x
     qring Q=std(xy-1);
     module M=imap(r,M);
     Ann(M);
     ==> _[1]=0


