D.4.28.2 primdecZM
..................

Procedure from library `primdecint.lib' (*note primdecint_lib::).

*Usage:*
     primdecZM(N); N module
     The coefficients must be ZZ.

*Return:*
     a list pr of primary modules and their associated primes:
        pr[i][1]   the i-th primary component,
        pr[i][2]   the i-th prime component.

*Example:*
     LIB "primdecint.lib";
     ring R=integer,(x,y),(c,lp);
     module N=[0,0,xy2-x2-xy],[0,y,x],[0,x,2xy-x],[x,0,-xy],[0,0,18x];
     primdecZM(N);
     ==> [1]:
     ==>    [1]:
     ==>       _[1]=[0,0,x]
     ==>       _[2]=[0,1]
     ==>       _[3]=[x]
     ==>    [2]:
     ==>       _[1]=x
     ==> [2]:
     ==>    [1]:
     ==>       _[1]=[0,0,y3]
     ==>       _[2]=[0,0,18x]
     ==>       _[3]=[0,0,xy2]
     ==>       _[4]=[0,0,x2+xy]
     ==>       _[5]=[0,y,x]
     ==>       _[6]=[0,x,2xy-x]
     ==>       _[7]=[y3]
     ==>       _[8]=[x,0,-xy]
     ==>    [2]:
     ==>       _[1]=y
     ==>       _[2]=x


