D.4.32.4 modJanet
.................

Procedure from library `rstandard.lib' (*note rstandard_lib::).

*Usage:*
     modJanet(I,i); I is an ideal, i an integer (optional).

*Return:*
     ideal, a Janet basis for I using modular methods.

*Purpose:*
     Computes a Janet basis for the ideal given by the generators in I
     using modular techniques.
     If second argument is 0 then the result is not verified.

*Example:*
     LIB "rstandard.lib";
     ring R=0,(t,x,y,z),ds;
     ideal i=
     5t3x2z+2t2y3x5,
     7y+4x2y+y2x+2zt,
     3tz+3yz2+2yz4;
     ideal j=modJanet(i);  j;
