D.5.4 divisors_lib
------------------

*Library:*
     divisors.lib

*Purpose:*
     Divisors and P-Divisors

*Authors:*
     Janko Boehm boehm@mathematik.uni-kl.de
     Lars Kastner kastner@math.fu-berlin.de
     Benjamin Lorenz blorenz@math.uni-frankfurt.de
     Hans Schoenemann hannes@mathematik.uni-kl.de
     Yue Ren ren@mathematik.uni-kl.de

*Overview:*
     We implement a class divisor on an algebraic variety and methods
     for computing with them. Divisors are represented by tuples of
     ideals defining the positive and the negative part. In particular,
     we implement the group structure on divisors, computing global
     sections and testing linear equivalence.

     In addition to this we provide a class formaldivisor which
     implements integer formal sums of divisors (not necessarily
     prime). A formal divisor can be evaluated to a divisor, and a
     divisor can be decomposed into a formal sum.

     Finally we provide a class pdivisor which implements polyhedral
     formal sums of divisors (P-divisors) where the coefficients are
     assumed to be polyhedra with fixed tail cone.  There is a function
     to evaluate a P-divisor on a vector in the dual of the tail cone.
     The result will be a formal divisor.

*References:*
     For the class divisor we closely follow Macaulay2's tutorial on
     divisors.


*Procedures:*

* Menu:

* makeDivisor:: create a divisor
* divisorplus:: add two divisors
* multdivisor:: multiply a divisor by an integer
* negativedivisor:: compute the negative of the divisor
* normalFormDivisor:: normal form of a divisor
* isEqualDivisor:: test whether two divisors are equal
* globalSections:: compute the global sections of a divisor
* degreeDivisor:: degree of a divisor
* linearlyEquivalent:: test whether two divisors a linearly equivalent
* effective:: compute an effective divisor linearly equivalent to a divisor
* makeFormalDivisor:: make a formal integer sum of divisors
* evaluateFormalDivisor:: evaluate a formal sum of divisors to a divisor
* formaldivisorplus:: add two formal divisors
* negativeformaldivisor:: compute the negative of the formal divisor
* multformaldivisor:: multiply a formal divisor by an integer
* degreeFormalDivisor:: degree of a formal divisor
* makePDivisor:: make a formal polyhedral sum of divisors


File: singular.info,  Node: makeDivisor,  Next: divisorplus,  Up: divisors_lib

D.5.4.1 makeDivisor
...................

Procedure from library `divisors.lib' (*note divisors_lib::).

*Usage:*
     makeDivisor(I ,J); I = ideal, J = ideal.
*Assume:*
     I and J are ideals in a qring Q of a smooth irreducible variety X
     such that any ideal in Q satisfies the S2 condition.

*Return:*
     a divisor on X

*Theory:*
     The procedure will eliminate all components which are not of
     codimension 1.  The S2 condition requires that every proper
     nonzero principal ideal has pure codimension 1.

*Example:*
     LIB "divisors.lib";
     ring r=31991,(x,y,z),dp;
     ideal I = y^2*z - x*(x-z)*(x+3*z);
     qring Q = std(I);
     divisor P = makeDivisor(ideal(x,z),ideal(1));


