Procedure from library `divisors.lib' (*note divisors_lib::).

*Usage:*
     divisorplus(A ,B); A + B; A = divisor, B = divisor.
*Assume:*
     A and B are divisors on X.

*Return:*
     a divisor on X

*Theory:*
     The procedure will compute the product of the numerator and
     denominator ideals, respectively.

*Example:*
     LIB "divisors.lib";
     ring r=31991,(x,y,z),dp;
     ideal I = y^2*z - x*(x-z)*(x+3*z);
     qring Q = std(I);
     divisor A = makeDivisor(ideal(x,z),ideal(1));
     divisor B = makeDivisor(ideal(x,y),ideal(1));
     A+B;
     ==> (x,yz) - (1)
     ==>


