D.5.4.3 multdivisor
...................

Procedure from library `divisors.lib' (*note divisors_lib::).

*Usage:*
     multdivisor(n ,A); A*n; n = integer, A = divisor.
*Assume:*
     n is an integer and A is a divisor on X.

*Return:*
     a divisor on X

*Theory:*
     The procedure will compute the n-th power of the numerator and
     denominator ideals, respectively.

*Example:*
     LIB "divisors.lib";
     ring r=31991,(x,y,z),dp;
     ideal I = y^2*z - x*(x-z)*(x+3*z);
     qring Q = std(I);
     divisor A = makeDivisor(ideal(x,z),ideal(1));
     A;
     ==> (z,x) - (1)
     ==>
     divisor D = multdivisor(4,A);
     D;
     ==> (z2,xz) - (1)
     ==>
     A*4;
     ==> (z2,xz) - (1)
     ==>


