D.5.4.5 normalFormDivisor
.........................

Procedure from library `divisors.lib' (*note divisors_lib::).

*Usage:*
     normalFormDivisor(A); A = divisor.
*Assume:*
     A is a divisor on X.

*Return:*
     different representative of the same divisor on X

*Theory:*
     The procedure will cancel common components of numerator and
     denominator.

*Example:*
     LIB "divisors.lib";
     ring r=31991,(x,y,z),dp;
     ideal I = y^2*z - x*(x-z)*(x+3*z);
     qring Q = std(I);
     divisor A = makeDivisor(ideal(x,z),ideal(1));
     divisor B = makeDivisor(ideal(x,y),ideal(1));
     divisor D = (A+B)+multdivisor(-1,B);
     D;
     ==> (x,yz) - (y,x)
     ==>
     normalFormDivisor(D);
     ==> (z,x) - (1)
     ==>


