D.5.17.1 makeVariety
....................

Procedure from library `schubert.lib' (*note schubert_lib::).

*Usage:*
     makeVariety(d,i); d int, i ideal

*Assume:*
     d is a nonnegative integer, i is an ideal

*Return:*
     variety

*Theory:*
     create an abstract variety which has dimension d, and its Chow ring
     should be a quotient ring

*Example:*
     LIB "schubert.lib";
     ring r = 0,(h,e),wp(1,1);
     ideal rels = he,h2+e2;
     variety V = makeVariety(2,rels);
     V;
     ==> A variety of dimension 2
     ==>
     V.dimension;
     ==> 2
     V.relations;
     ==> _[1]=he
     ==> _[2]=h2+e2


