D.5.17.33 homog_part
....................

Procedure from library `schubert.lib' (*note schubert_lib::).

*Usage:*
     homog_part(f,n); f poly, n int

*Return:*
     poly

*Purpose:*
     computing the homogeneous component of a polynomial.

*Example:*
     LIB "schubert.lib";
     ring r = 0,(x,y,z),wp(1,2,3);
     poly f = 1+x+x2+x3+x4+y+y2+y3+z+z2+xy+xz+yz+xyz;
     homog_part(f,0);
     ==> 1
     homog_part(f,1);
     ==> x
     homog_part(f,2);
     ==> x2+y
     homog_part(f,3);
     ==> x3+xy+z
     homog_part(f,4);
     ==> x4+y2+xz
     homog_part(f,5);
     ==> yz
     homog_part(f,6);
     ==> y3+xyz+z2


