D.11.2.5 leftKernel
...................

Procedure from library `control.lib' (*note control_lib::).

*Usage:*
     leftKernel(M); M a matrix

*Return:*
     module

*Purpose:*
     computes left kernel of matrix M (a module of all elements v such
     that vM=0)

*Example:*
     LIB "control.lib";
     ring r= 0,(x,y,z),dp;
     matrix M[3][1] = x,y,z;
     print(M);
     ==> x,
     ==> y,
     ==> z
     matrix L = leftKernel(M);
     print(L);
     ==> 0, -z,y,
     ==> -y,x, 0,
     ==> -z,0, x
     // check:
     print(L*M);
     ==> 0,
     ==> 0,
     ==> 0


