D.11.2.9 colrank
................

Procedure from library `control.lib' (*note control_lib::).

*Usage:*
     colrank(M); M a matrix/module

*Return:*
     int

*Purpose:*
     compute the column rank of M as of matrix

*Note_*
     this procedure uses Bareiss algorithm

*Example:*
     LIB "control.lib";
     // de Rham complex
     ring r=0,(D(1..3)),dp;
     module R;
     R=[0,-D(3),D(2)],
     [D(3),0,-D(1)],
     [-D(2),D(1),0];
     R=transpose(R);
     colrank(R);
     ==> 2


