D.11.4 findifs_lib
------------------

*Library:*
     findifs.lib

*Purpose:*
     Tools for the finite difference schemes

*Authors:*
     Viktor Levandovskyy, levandov@math.rwth-aachen.de

*Overview:*
     We provide the presentation of difference operators in a
     polynomial, semi-factorized and a nodal form. Running
     `findifs_example();' will demonstrate, how we generate finite
     difference schemes of linear PDEs from given approximations.

     Theory: The method we use have been developed by V. Levandovskyy
     and Bernd Martin. The computation of a finite difference scheme of
     a given single linear partial differential equation with constant
     coefficients with a given approximation rules boils down to the
     computation of a Groebner basis of a submodule of a free module
     with respect to the ordering, eliminating module components.

     Support: SpezialForschungsBereich F1301 of the Austrian FWF


*Procedures:*

* Menu:

* findifs_example:: contains a guided explanation of our approach
* decoef:: decompose polynomial P into summands with respect to the number n
* difpoly2tex:: present the difference scheme in the nodal form
* exp2pt:: convert a polynomial M into the TeX format, in nodal form
* texcoef:: converts the number n into TeX
* npar:: search for 'n' among the parameters and returns its number
* magnitude:: compute the square of the magnitude of a complex expression
* replace:: replace in s all the substrings with a given string
* xchange:: exchange two substrings in a given string

* Menu:

See also:
* finitediff_lib::
* latex_lib::


