D.13.7.1 setUniformizingParameter
.................................

Procedure from library `tropicalNewton.lib' (*note
tropicalNewton_lib::).

*Usage:*
     setUniformizingParameter(p); p number

*Return:*
     none, sets the uniformizing parameter as p

*Assume:*
     char(K)==0 and p prime number or
     trdeg(K)>0 and p transcendental variable or
     p==0

*Example:*
     LIB "tropicalNewton.lib";
     // poor man's polynomials over Puiseux series:
     ring r = (0,t),x,dp;
     setUniformizingParameter(t);
     val(t2+t3);
     ==> 2
     val(t^-2+t^-3);
     ==> -3
     // poor man's polynomials over p-adic numbers:
     ring s = 0,x,dp;
     setUniformizingParameter(2);
     val(12);
     ==> 2
     val(1/12);
     ==> -2


