D.14.1 arr_lib
--------------

*Library:*
     arr.lib

*Purpose:*
     a library of algorithms for arrangements of hyperplanes

*Authors:*
     Randolf Scholz (rscholz@rhrk.uni-kl.de),
     Patrick Serwene (serwene@mathematik.uni-kl.de),
     Lukas Kuehne (lf.kuehne@gmail.com)

*Overloads:*
     // OPERATORS
     = arrAdd assignment
     + arrAdd union of two arrs
     [ arrGet access to a single/multiple hyperplane(s) - arrMinus
     deletes given hyperplanes from the arr <= arrLEQ comparison
     >= arrGEQ comparison
     == arrEQ comparison
     != arrNEQ comparison
     < arrLNEQ comparison
     > arrGNEQ comparison

     // TYPECASTING
     matrix arr2mat coeff matrix
     poly arr2poly defining polynomial

     // OTHER
     variables arrVariables ideal generated by the variables the arr
     depends on nvars arrNvars number of variables the arr depends on
     delete arrDelete deletes hyperplanes by indices print arrPrint
     prints the arr on the screen

     // IDEAL INHERITED FUNCTIONS
     homog arrHomog checks if arrangement is homogeneous simplify
     arrSimplify simplifies arrangement size arrSize number of planes
     subst arrSubst substitute variables

     // MULTI-ARRANGEMENTS
     = multarrAdd assignment of multarr
     + multarrAdd union of multarr
     poly multarr2poly defining polynomial
     size multarrSize number of hyperplanes with mult.  print
     multarrPrint displays multiarr
     delete multarrDelete deletes hyperplane


*Procedures:*

* Menu:

* arrSet:: replaces the k-th Hyperplane with poly p
* type2arr:: converts general input to 'arr' using arrAdd.
* mat2arr:: affine arrangement from coeff matrix
* mat2carr:: central arrangement from coeff matrix
* arrPrintMatrix:: readable output as a coeff matrix
* varMat:: matrix of the corresponding ring_variables
* varNum:: number of given variable (enh. version of varNum in dmod.lib)
* arrSwapVar:: swaps two variables in the arrangement
* arrLastVar:: ring_variable of largest index used in arrangement
* arrCenter:: computes center of an arrangement
* arrCentral:: checks if arrangement is central
* arrCentered:: checks if arrangement is centered
* arrCentralize:: makes centered arrangement central
* arrCoordChange:: performs coordinate change
* arrCoordNormalize:: performs projection onto coordinate hyperplane
* arrCone:: coned arrangement
* arrDecone:: deconed arrangement
* arrLocalize:: localization of an arrangement onto a flat
* arrRestrict:: restricted arrangement onto a flat
* arrIsEssential:: checks if arrangement is essential
* arrEssentialize:: essentialized arragnement
* arrBoolean:: boolean arrangement
* arrBraid:: braid arrangement
* arrTypeB:: type B arrangement
* arrTypeD:: type D arrangement
* arrRandom:: random (affine) arrangement
* arrRandomCentral:: random central arrangement
* arrEdelmanReiner:: Edelman-Reiner arrangement
* arrOrlikSolomon:: Orlik-Solomon algebra of the arrangement
* arrDer:: module of derivation
* arrIsFree:: checks if arrangement is free
* arrExponents:: exponents of a (free) arrangement
* arr2multarr:: converts normal arrangement to multiarrangement
* multarr2arr:: converts multiarrangement to normal arrangement
* multarrRestrict:: restriction of A (as arr) to a flat with multiplicities
* multarrMultRestrict:: restriction of A (as multarr) to a hyperplane with multiplicities
