D.14.1.12 arrCentered
.....................

Procedure from library `arr.lib' (*note arr_lib::).

*Usage:*
     arrCentered(A); arr A

*Return:*
     [0,1] true if A is centered(i.e. intersection of all planes not
     empty)

*Note_*
     The algorithm uses the rank of matrix: Ax=b has a solution iff
     rank(A) = rank(A|b)

*Example:*
     LIB "arr.lib";
     ring R = 0,(x,y,z),dp;
     arr A= ideal(x,y,x-y+1);        // centerless
     arrCentral(A);
     ==> 0
     arr B= ideal(x,y,z);            // central with center being the origin
     arrCentral(B);
     ==> 1
     arr C= ideal(x+1,2y+1,-z+1);    // central with center (-1,-1/2, 1)
     arrCentral(C);
     ==> 0

