D.14.1.17 arrDecone
...................

Procedure from library `arr.lib' (*note arr_lib::).

*Usage:*
     arrDecone(A, k); arrangement A, integer k;

*Return:*
     arr: the deconed hyperplane Arrangement dA

*Note_*
     A has to be non-empty and central. arrDecone is an inverse
     operation to arrCone since A == arrDecone(arrCone(A),size(A)+1)
     for any A.  One can also decone a central arrangement with respect
     to any hyper- plane k, but than a coordinate change is necessary
     to make H_k = ker(x_k). Since such a coordinate change is not
     unique, use arrCoordchange to do so.

*Example:*
     LIB "arr.lib";
     ring R = 0,(x,y,z),dp;
     arr A= ideal(x,y,z,x+y-z);
     arrDecone(A,3);
     ==> _[1]=x
     ==> _[2]=y
     ==> _[3]=x+y-1
     ==>

