*Library:*
     methods.lib

*Purpose:*
     installing methods in Singular

*Authors:*
     J. Boehm, boehm @ mathematik.uni-kl.de

*Overview:*
     Methods select the function to execute by the types of the input
     tuple.  The central function is installMethod, which takes a
     hashtable associating a tuple of input types to function names and
     creates a corresponding procedure.

     HashTables are lists with arbitrary index sets. They can be
     created by the command hashTable. Their size can be determined by
     the command size. Values can be extracted by selectKey or the *
     operator. HashTables can also be added using addHashTables or the
     + operator.

     Methods can be added with the + operator.

*Types:*
     Method the class of all methods
     HashTable the class of all hash tables


