D.14.7.1 boolean_std
....................

Procedure from library `polybori.lib' (*note polybori_lib::).

*Usage:*
     boolean_std(Is); Is ideal

*Return:*
     Singular ideal of the boolean groebner basis of Is

*Example:*
     LIB "polybori.lib";
     ring r0=2,x(1..4),lp;
     poly f1=x(1)^2+2*x(2)*(x(3))-x(4)^3;
     poly f2=x(1)^2-x(3)*x(1);
     poly f3=x(2)+5-2*x(1);
     poly f4=x(1)*x(2)-x(3);
     ideal I=f1,f2,f3,f4;
     boolean_std(I);        // implicitly add x(i)^2-x(i)
     bideal bI=I;           // alternative syntax
     bideal re = std(bI);  // Continue PolyBoRi computations
     std(re[1..2]);
     ring r1=0,x,Dp;
     poly f1=x3+2*x+1;
     poly f2=x10-x5+2x;
     poly f3=19;
     ideal I=f1,f2,f3;
     boolean_std(I);
     ring r2=32003,(x,y,z),Dp;
     poly f1=xz+y+20*x^2*y;
     poly f2=32002*xy+xz2+y;
     ideal I=f1,f2;
     boolean_std(I);
     ring r2=32003,(x,y,z),Dp;
     poly f1=xyz+20*x^2*y-3*xz+15;
     poly f2=32002*xy+z2;
     poly f3=19*x5y;
     ideal I=f1,f2,f3;
     boolean_std(I);

