D.15.3.18 difformDiv
....................

Procedure from library `difform.lib' (*note difform_lib::).

*Usage:*
     df/dg; df,dg difform

*Return:*
     the quotient df/dg as differential form

*Example:*
     LIB "difform.lib";
     ring R = 0,(x,y,z),lp;
     diffAlgebra();
     ==> // The differential algebra Omega_R was constructed and the differential \
        forms dDx, dDy, dDz, dx, dy, dz are available.
     /////////////////////////////////
     // Divisions without remainder //
     /////////////////////////////////
     dx / dx;
     ==> 1
     ==>
     dx*dy*dz / dz;
     ==> dx*dy
     ==>
     (dx*x2 - yx2) / x2;
     ==> -y+dx
     ==>
     //////////////////////////////
     // Divisions with reaminder //
     //////////////////////////////
     (dx + dx*dy + 1) / dx;
     ==> 1+(-1)*dy
     ==>
     (x2*dx - x*dy) / (dx-dy);
     ==> x2
     ==>
     kill Omega_R,dx,dy,dz;

* Menu:

See also:
* difformMul::


