D.15.3.24 difformIsHomog
........................

Procedure from library `difform.lib' (*note difform_lib::).

*Usage:*
     homog(df); df difform

*Return:*
     1, if df is homogeneous - 0, otherwise

*Note_*
     - the form 0 is homogeneous
     - be careful: difformIsHomog does not cast polynomials to
     differential forms. So before applying to a polynomial, a type
     cast should be done

*Example:*
     LIB "difform.lib";
     ring R = 0,(x,y,z),ds;
     diffAlgebra();
     ==> // The differential algebra Omega_R was constructed and the differential \
        forms dDx, dDy, dDz, dx, dy, dz are available.
     /////////////////
     // Homogeneous //
     /////////////////
     homog(3*dx*dz - x8*dx*dy);
     ==> 0
     homog(12x*dx + dy - (y4-y5)*dz);
     ==> 0
     /////////////////////
     // Not homogeneous //
     /////////////////////
     homog(3 + x8*dy);
     ==> 0
     homog(x*dx+dy*dx);
     ==> 0
     // When applying homog to a polynomial which is considered
     // as a differential form, a type cast has to be done first
     homog(3x-y2);
     ==> 0
     difform df = 3x-y2;
     homog(df);
     ==> 1
     kill Omega_R,dx,dy,dz,df;

* Menu:

See also:
* difformDeg::
* difformIsHomogDeg::


