D.15.5.3 scheme
...............

Procedure from library `finitediff.lib' (*note finitediff_lib::).

*Usage:*
     scheme([v1,..,vn]); v1,..,vn of type vector

*Return:*
     poly

*Purpose:*
     performs substitutions by the means of Groebner basis computation
     of the submodule, generated by the input vectors, then intersects
     the intermediate result with the suitable component in order to
     get a finite difference scheme

*Note_*
     works only for a single PDE, for the case of a system use
     `matrixsystem'

*Example:*
     LIB "finitediff.lib";
     list D="Ux","Ut","U";
     list P="a";
     list V="t","x";
     setinitials(V,D,P);
     def s1=scheme(u(Ut)+a*u(Ux),backward(Ux,U,x),forward(Ut,U,t));
     s1;
     ==> (-a*dt+dx)/(dx)*x+(a*dt)/(dx)


