D.15.7 gradedModules_lib
------------------------

*Library:*
     gradedModules.lib

*Purpose:*
     Operations with graded modules/matrices/resolutions

*Authors:*
     Oleksandr Motsak <U@D>, where U=motsak, D=mathematik.uni-kl.de
     Hanieh Keneshlou <hkeneshlou@yahoo.com>

*Overview:*
     The library contains several procedures for constructing and
     manipulating graded modules/matrices/resolutions.  Basics about
     graded objects can be found in [DL].
     Throughout this library graded objects are graded maps, that is,
     matrices with polynomials, together with grading weights for
     source and destination. Graded modules are implicitly given as
     coker of a graded map.  Note that in special cases we may also
     consider submodules in S^r generated by columns of a graded
     polynomial matrix (or a graded map).

*Note_*
     set assumeLevel to positive integer value in order to auto-check
     all assumptions.  We denote the current basering by S.

*References:*
     [DL] Decker, W., Lossen, Ch.: Computing in Algebraic Geometry,
     Springer, 2006


*Procedures:*

* Menu:

* grobj:: construct a graded object (map) given by matrix M
* grtest:: check whether A is a valid graded object
* grdeg:: compute graded degrees of columns of the map M
* grview:: view the graded structure of map M
* grshift:: shift graded module coker(M) by +d
* grzero:: presentation of S(0)^1
* grtwist:: presentation of S(d)^r
* grtwists:: presentation of S(v[1])+...+S(v[size(v)])
* grsum:: direct sum of two graded modules coker(M) + coker(N)
* grpower:: direct p-th power of graded module coker(M)
* grtranspose:: un-ordered graded transpose of map M
* grgens:: try to compute submodule generators of coker(M)
* grpres:: presentation of submodule generated by columns of F
* grorder:: reorder cols/rows of M for correct graded-block-structure
* grtranspose1:: reordered graded transpose of map M
* TestGRRes:: compute/order/transpose a graded resolution of ideal I
* KeneshlouMatrixPresentation:: build some presentation with intvec v
* grsyz:: syzygy of Im(M)
* grres:: resolution of Im(M) of length l... minimal?
* grlift:: graded lift, gens!
* grprod:: composition of graded maps (product of matrices?)
* grgroebner:: Groebner Basis of Im(M) as a graded object
* grconcat:: sum of maps into the same target module
* grrndmat:: generate random matrix compatible with src and dst gradings
* grrndmap:: generate random 0-deg homomorphism src(S) -> src(D)
* grrndmap2:: generate random 0-deg homomorphism dst(S) -> dst(D)
* grlifting:: RND! chain lifting
* grlifting2:: RND! chain lifting
* mappingcone:: mapping cone?
* grlifting3:: RND! chain lifting? probably wrong one
* mappingcone3:: mapping cone3?
* grrange:: get the row-weightings
* grneg:: graded object given by -A
* matrixpres:: matrix presentation of direct sum of Omega^{a[i]}(i)


