     multIdeals(f);
     ==> [1]:
     ==>    [1]:
     ==>       _[1]=1
     ==>    [2]:
     ==>       5/6
     ==>    [3]:
     ==>       1
     ==> [2]:
     ==>    [1]:
     ==>       _[1]=y
     ==>       _[2]=x
     ==>    [2]:
     ==>       1
     ==>    [3]:
     ==>       1


File: singular.info,  Node: nextHodgeIdeal,  Prev: multIdeals,  Up: hodge_lib

D.15.8.4 nextHodgeIdeal
.......................

Procedure from library `hodge.lib' (*note hodge_lib::).

*Usage:*
     nextHodgeIdeal(f, I, p); f a poly, I an ideal, p a non-negative
     integer

*Return:*
     ideal

*Purpose:*
     given the p -th Hodge ideal I  of f^\alpha  compute the p+1 -th
     Hodge ideal assuming that
     the Hodge filtration of the underlying mixed Hodge module is
     generated at level less than or equal to p .

*Example:*
     LIB "hodge.lib";
     ring R = 0,(x,y),dp;
     poly f = y^2-x^3;
     def Ra = hodgeIdeals(f, 2);
     setring(Ra);
     int p = 1;
     nextHodgeIdeal(y^2-x^3, hodge[3][1][p+1], p);
     ==> _[1]=x^2*y^2
     ==> _[2]=y^3
     ==> _[3]=x^3*y
     ==> _[4]=x^4+(2*a+1)*x*y^2


