D.15.12.3 modfWalk
..................

Procedure from library `modwalk.lib' (*note modwalk_lib::).

*Return:*
     a standard basis of I

*Note_*
     The procedure computes a standard basis of I (over the rational
     numbers) by using modular methods.

*Example:*
     LIB "modwalk.lib";
     ring R1 = 0, (x,y,z,t), dp;
     ideal I = 3x3+x2+1, 11y5+y3+2, 5z4+z2+4;
     I = std(I);
     ring R2 = 0, (x,y,z,t), lp;
     ideal I = fetch(R1, I);
     ideal J = modfWalk(I);
     J;
     ==> J[1]=z4+1/5z2+4/5
     ==> J[2]=y5+1/11y3+2/11
     ==> J[3]=x3+1/3x2+1/3
     ring S1 = 0, (a,b,c,d), Dp;
     ideal I = 5b2, ac2+9d3+3a2+5b, 2a2c+7abd+bcd+4a2, 2ad2+6b2d+7c3+8ad+4c;
     I = std(I);
     ring S2 = 0, (c,d,b,a), lp;
     ideal I = fetch(S1,I);
     // I is assumed to be a Dp-Groebner basis.
     // We compute a lp-Groebner basis.
     ideal J = modfWalk(I,"Dp");
     J;
