D.15.13 multigrading_lib
------------------------

Todos/Issues:
   * See `http://code.google.com/p/convex-singular/wiki/Multigrading'

*Library:*
     multigrading.lib

*Purpose:*
     Multigraded Rings

*Authors:*
     Benjamin Bechtold, benjamin.bechtold@googlemail.com
     Rene Birkner, rbirkner@math.fu-berlin.de
     Lars Kastner, lkastner@math.fu-berlin.de
     Simon Keicher, keicher@mail.mathematik.uni-tuebingen.de
     Oleksandr Motsak, U@D, where U={motsak}, D={mathematik.uni-kl.de}
     Anna-Lena Winz, anna-lena.winz@math.fu-berlin.de

*Overview:*
     This library allows one to virtually add multigradings to Singular:
     grade multivariate polynomial rings with arbitrary (fin. gen.
     Abelian) groups.  For more see
     http://code.google.com/p/convex-singular/wiki/Multigrading For
     theoretical references see:
     E. Miller, B. Sturmfels: 'Combinatorial Commutative Algebra' and
     M. Kreuzer, L. Robbiano: 'Computational Commutative Algebra'.

*Note_*
     'multiDegBasis' relies on 4ti2 for computing Hilbert Bases.  All
     groups are finitely generated Abelian


*Procedures:*

* Menu:

* setBaseMultigrading:: attach multiweights/grading group matrices to the basering
* getVariableWeights:: get matrix of multidegrees of vars attached to a ring
* getGradingGroup:: get grading group attached to a ring
* getLattice:: get grading group' lattice attached to a ring (or its NF)
* createGroup:: create a group generated by S, with relations L
* createQuotientGroup:: create a group generated by the unit matrix with relations L
* createTorsionFreeGroup:: create a group generated by S which is torsionfree
* printGroup:: print a group
* isGroup:: test whether G is a valid group
* isGroupHomomorphism:: test whether A defines a group homomrphism from L1 to L2
* isGradedRingHomomorphism:: test graded ring homomorph
* createGradedRingHomomorphism:: create a graded ring homomorph
* setModuleGrading:: attach multiweights of units to a module and return it
* getModuleGrading:: get multiweights of module units (attached to M)
* isSublattice:: test whether A is a sublattice of B
* imageLattice:: computes an integral basis for P(L)
* intRank:: computes the rank of the intmat A
* kernelLattice:: computes an integral basis for the kernel of the linear map P.
* latticeBasis:: computes an integral basis of the lattice B
* preimageLattice:: computes an integral basis for the preimage of the lattice L under the linear map P.
* projectLattice:: computes a linear map of lattices having the primitive span of B as its kernel.
* intersectLattices:: computes an integral basis for the intersection of the lattices A and B.
* isIntegralSurjective:: test whether the map P of lattices is surjective.
* isPrimitiveSublattice:: test whether A generates a primitive sublattice.
* intInverse:: computes the integral inverse matrix of the intmat A
* integralSection:: for a given linear surjective map P of lattices this procedure returns an integral section of P.
* primitiveSpan:: computes a basis for the minimal primitive sublattice that contains the given vectors (by A).
* factorgroup:: create the group G mod H
* productgroup:: create the group G x H
* multiDeg:: compute the multidegree of A
* multiDegBasis:: compute all monomials of multidegree d
* multiDegPartition:: compute the multigraded-homogeneous components of p
* isTorsionFree:: test whether the current multigrading is free
* isPositive:: test whether the current multigrading is positive
* isZeroElement:: test whether p has zero multidegree
* areZeroElements:: test whether an integer matrix M considered as a collection of columns has zero multidegree
* isHomogeneous:: test whether 'a' is multigraded-homogeneous
* equalMultiDeg:: test whether e1==e2 in the current multigrading
* multiDegGroebner:: compute the multigraded GB/SB of M
* multiDegSyzygy:: compute the multigraded syzygies of M
* multiDegModulo:: compute the multigraded 'modulo' module of I and J
* multiDegResolution:: compute the multigraded resolution of M
* multiDegTensor:: compute the tensor product of multigraded modules m,n
* multiDegTor:: compute the Tor_i(m,n) for multigraded modules m,n
* defineHomogeneous:: get a grading group wrt which p becomes homogeneous
* pushForward:: find the finest grading on the image ring, homogenizing f
* gradiator:: coarsens grading of the ring until h becomes homogeneous
* hermiteNormalForm:: compute the Hermite Normal Form of a matrix
* smithNormalForm:: compute matrices D,P,Q with D=P*A*Q and D is the smith normal form of A
* hilbertSeries:: compute the multigraded Hilbert Series of M
* lll:: applies LLL(.) of lll.lib which only works for lists on a matrix A


