D.15.13.35 isZeroElement
........................

Procedure from library `multigrading.lib' (*note multigrading_lib::).

*Usage:*
     isZeroElement(d, [T]); intvec d, group T

*Purpose:*
     For a integer vector 'd' representing the multidegree of some
     polynomial or vector this method computes if the multidegree is
     contained in the grading group group (either set globally or given
     as an optional argument), i.e. if it is zero in the multigrading.

*Example:*
     LIB "multigrading.lib";
     ring r = 0,(x,y,z),dp;
     intmat g[2][3]=
     1,0,1,
     0,1,1;
     intmat t[2][1]=
     -2,
     1;
     intmat tt[2][1]=
     1,
     -1;
     setBaseMultigrading(g,t);
     poly a = x10yz;
     poly b = x8y2z;
     poly c = x4z2;
     poly d = y5;
     poly e = x2y2;
     poly f = z2;
     intvec v1 = multiDeg(a) - multiDeg(b);
     v1;
     ==> 2,-1
     isZeroElement(v1);
     ==> 1
     isZeroElement(v1, tt);
     ==> 0
     intvec v2 = multiDeg(a) - multiDeg(c);
     v2;
     ==> 5,0
     isZeroElement(v2);
     ==> 0
     isZeroElement(v2, tt);
     ==> 0
     intvec v3 = multiDeg(e) - multiDeg(f);
     v3;
     ==> 0,0
     isZeroElement(v3);
     ==> 1
     isZeroElement(v3, tt);
     ==> 1
     intvec v4 = multiDeg(c) - multiDeg(d);
     v4;
     ==> 6,-3
     isZeroElement(v4);
     ==> 1
     isZeroElement(v4, tt);
     ==> 0


