D.15.14.4 displaypfd
....................

Procedure from library `pfd.lib' (*note pfd_lib::).

*Usage:*
     displaypfd(dec); dec list

*Purpose:*
     print a partial fraction decomposition `dec' in a readable way.
     The list `dec' has to have the same structure as the output of
     *note pfd::.

*Example:*
     LIB "pfd.lib";
     ring R = 0,(x,y),dp;
     poly f = x^3+3*x^2*y+2*y^2-x^2+4*x*y;
     poly g = x^2*y*(x-1)*(x-y)^2;
     list dec = pfd(f,g);
     ==>   (2) / (q3*q4)
     ==> + (-2) / (q1*q4)
     ==> + (-6) / (q3*q4^2)
     ==> + (1) / (q2*q4^2)
     ==> + (9) / (q1*q4^2)
     ==> + (2) / (q3^2*q4)
     ==> where
     ==> q1 = x-1
     ==> q2 = y
     ==> q3 = x
     ==> q4 = x-y
     ==> (6 terms)
     ==>
     displaypfd(dec);
     ==>   (2) / (q3*q4)
     ==> + (-2) / (q1*q4)
     ==> + (-6) / (q3*q4^2)
     ==> + (1) / (q2*q4^2)
     ==> + (9) / (q1*q4^2)
     ==> + (2) / (q3^2*q4)
     ==> where
     ==> q1 = x-1
     ==> q2 = y
     ==> q3 = x
     ==> q4 = x-y
     ==> (6 terms)
     ==>

