D.15.22.3 makeQPoly
...................

Procedure from library `stanleyreisner.lib' (*note
stanleyreisner_lib::).

*Usage:*
     makeQPoly(p); p = polynomial.

*Assume:*
     p is a polynomial in basering.

*Return:*
     a QPoly which is in a quotient ring.

*Theory:*
     The procedure will convert a polynomial in basering to a
     polynomial in a quotient ring.

*Example:*
     LIB "stanleyreisner.lib";
     ring r=0,(x,y,z),lp;
     ideal i=xy;
     qring Q=std(i);
     poly p=x*y+z;
     QPoly q=makeQPoly(p);
     q.over;
     ==> // coefficients: QQ considered as a field
     ==> // number of vars : 3
     ==> //        block   1 : ordering lp
     ==> //                  : names    x y z
     ==> //        block   2 : ordering C
     ==> // quotient ring from ideal
     ==> _[1]=xy
     q.value;
     ==> z


