D.15.29.1 applyVecField
.......................

Procedure from library `VecField.lib' (*note VecField_lib::).

*Usage:*
     applyVecField(VecField V, poly/ideal p [,int n])

*Return:*
     if p is a polynomial, return a polynomial V(p), if p is an ideal,
     the ideal V(p).  If an optional n is given, only the parts of V up
     to and including degree n are applied to p.

*Example:*
     LIB "VecField.lib";
     int oldp = printlevel;
     printlevel = 1;
     ring r = 0, (x, y, z),ds;
     vector v = [-1,-1,-1];
     VecField V = v;
     poly f = x3+2y3+xz2;
     poly g = V*f;
     ideal I = (x2,y);
     ideal J = V*I;
     printlevel = oldp;


