News for version 4-0-0
======================

Version 4-0-0 is a milestone release of Singular.  The new release
series 4 aims for an entirely modularized architecture simplifying
connectivity with other systems and paving the way for parallel
computations.  As  a first step in modularization, the new  release
features an internal structural separation of coefficient rings and
polynomial rings.  This allows for a flexible integration of new
coefficient rings.

SINGULAR 4-0-0's list of new functionality and significant improvements
further extends that of the 3-1-6/7 prerelease series.

New functionality

   * de Rham cohomology of complements of algebraic varieties (*note
     deRham_lib::)

   * Gromov-Witten numbers of elliptic curves (*note
     ellipticcovers_lib::)

   * classification of isolated complete intersection singularities in
     characteristic 0 (*note classifyci_lib::)

   * parametrization of orbits of unipotent actions (*note
     orbitparam_lib::)

   * F5-like Groebner basis algorithm (*note sba::)

   * element-wise application of functions to data structures (*note
     apply::)

   * support for debugging libraries (*note ASSUME::)

Improved functionality

   * Groebner cover for parametric ideals (*note grobcov_lib::)

   * normalization of affine rings (*note normal_lib::)

   * classification of real singularities (*note realclassify_lib::)

   * GIT-fans (*note gitfan_lib::)

   * algebraic/transcendental field extensions

   * *note Non-commutative subsystem::

   * an abstraction layer for parallel computations (*note
     parallel_lib::)

   * run-time loading of supplementary kernel code (*note Dynamic
     modules::)

   * interpreter language support for name spaces (*note package::)

Availability

SINGULAR is available as source code and for Linux, Mac OS X, Windows,
FreeBSD and SunOS-5.


